<h2 id="proetale-section-finite" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="09A7">61.24</span> Finite morphisms and pro-étale sites</h2>

<p>
It is not clear that a finite morphism of schemes determines an exact pushforward on abelian pro-étale sheaves. 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-lemma" id="09A8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09A8">Lemma <span data-tag="09A8">61.24.1</span>.</a> Let $f : Z \to X$ be a finite morphism of schemes which is locally of finite presentation. Then $f_{{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}, *} : \textit{Ab}(Z_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}) \to \textit{Ab}(X_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale})$ is exact. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The prove this we may work (Zariski) locally on $X$ and assume that $X$ is affine, say $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$. Then $Z = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$ for some finite $A$-algebra $B$ of finite presentation. The construction in the proof of Proposition <a href="/tag/0983" data-tag="0983">61.11.3</a> produces a faithfully flat, ind-étale ring map $A \to D$ with $D$ w-contractible. We may check exactness of a sequence of sheaves by evaluating on $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(D)$ be such an object. Then $f_{{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}, *}\mathcal{F}$ evaluated at $U$ is equal to $\mathcal{F}$ evaluated at $V = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(D \otimes _ A B)$. Since $D \otimes _ A B$ is w-contractible by Lemma <a href="/tag/0986" data-tag="0986">61.11.6</a> evaluation at $V$ is exact. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
